{"schemaVersion":1,"release":"20261119-seitz1","source":{"file":"dist/data/space-groups.json","upstreamCommit":"7b43201ac0973333edbe69bc3dd6ccb308abf624"},"courseRoute":"classroom/crystal?lesson=space-01&track=space","counts":{"spaceGroups":230,"representatives":2609,"products":52381,"nonzeroShifts":15636},"conventions":{"basis":"BC primitive direct fractional coordinates, active column-vector action. The right factor acts first.","data":"Exact integer linear parts and translations in twelfths from the ordinary space-group table. The group product returns the full translation, the chosen representative and their integer lattice shift.","momentum":"The active translation phase on a specified output Bloch state is exp(-2 pi i k dot L). The workshop uses exact quarter-grid coordinates and can test preservation modulo a reciprocal lattice vector.","scope":"A finite quotient workshop using the fixed BC representatives. A listed fractional offset alone cannot diagnose symmorphicity. The optional calculator transfer opens the chosen ordinary space group and wave vector for manual calculation."},"sources":[{"title":"Seitz symbols for crystallographic symmetry operations","url":"https://journals.iucr.org/a/issues/2014/03/00/es0405/index.html"},{"title":"Crystallographic shelves: space-group hierarchy explained","url":"https://journals.iucr.org/j/issues/2018/05/00/in5013/index.html"}],"files":{".github/workflows/pages.yml":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":1882,"sha256":"6f7db8d1ab7b15607b19324fd10c24c8c7f1d4f816779cff2702576f4426ca21"},"GOAL-ROADMAP.md":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":60436,"sha256":"64cbdfdcace1794e6395baa84d60ea53d73bd76b6568e6d020d62d4fa5941ff5"},"dist/app.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":99585,"sha256":"310f87d76b810f66a4282dc89b76f813234bf7b6e9769f0512bc8941bb315f62"},"dist/classroom-ui.js":{"normalization":"utf8-lf-v1","bytes":32231,"sha256":"4c213cbe9ee4b50963727d37c4fae8c44e6ac678e231125a13838992a785d6e4"},"dist/crystal-notation.js